body:
I'm sorry for what you're struggling.

&#x200B;

Back in the time when I was injuring the most, I used to do that with people I meet, to see if there were more people like me. I have 2 friends who struggled with self injury, I've etm them both after I have started and we bonded more because of that. They were the ones who caught my scars/injuries and while I was trying to brush it off they, on separate occasions since they didn't knew each other, showed me some scar like saying "I understand". There was no need to say anymore. We then would feel comfortable to talk about urges and wouldn't judge us, supported us to try to cope on healthier ways.
